  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Located at the far south of Pampelonne beach, the Bonne Terrasse cove was the stronghold of Ramatuelle's fishermen and remains little known to the general public, according to the tourist office. It forms an arc-shaped strip of sand 150 metres long; access is via steps (about 10 minutes from the car park). The beach is not supervised.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Ramatuelle tourist office states (FAQ consulted 29 October 2026) that all the town's beaches, including the Bonne Terrasse cove, are open to dogs on a leash, with no time slot announced.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: access is via steps (about 10 minutes from the car park): check that your dog is comfortable with steps and bring water for him, as no water point is reported.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The coastal path continues to <a href="/en/fiche-ramatuelle">La Douane beach</a>, where the tourist office points out a customs house built under Napoleon I and recently restored, then to <a href="/en/fiche-plage-cap-taillat">Cap Taillat</a> — a nice walk to extend the day on foot with your dog.</p>
    </div>

